        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 23:4",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "As at the report concerning Egypt, so shall they be sorely pained at the report of Tyre.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2,
            "text": "OR When the report is heard by Egypt."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 37
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 23:5",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Pass ye over to Tarshish; howl, ye inhabitants of the isle.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 23:6",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Is this your joyous city, whose antiquity is of ancient days? her own feet shall carry her afar off to sojourn.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2
          },
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 25
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 23:7",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Who hath taken this counsel against Tyre, the crowning city, whose merchants are princes, whose traffickers are the honourable of the earth?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 88,
            "text": "Ezek. 26:16."
          },
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 107,
            "text": "IE traders."
          },
          {
            "start": 116,
            "end": 126,
            "text": "HEB ones honored, i.e., famous."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 60
          },
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 80
          },
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 111
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Ezek. 26:16.",
            "prettyString": "Ezekiel 26:16",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "ezekiel",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 26,
                    "end": 26,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 16,
                        "end": 16
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 23:8",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "The Lord of hosts hath purposed it, to stain the pride of all glory, and to bring into contempt all the honourable of the earth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 72
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 23:9",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "Pass through thy land as a river, O daughter of Tarshish: there is no more strength.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 66
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 23:10",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "He stretched out his hand over the sea, he shook the kingdoms: the Lord hath given a commandment against the merchant city, to destroy the strong holds thereof.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 122,
            "text": "OR concerning Canaan."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 118,
            "end": 122
          },
          {
            "start": 122,
            "end": 123
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 23:11",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And he said, Thou shalt no more rejoice, O thou oppressed virgin, daughter of Zidon: arise, pass over to Chittim; there also shalt thou have no rest.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 23:12",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold the land of the Chaldeans; this people was not, till the Assyrian founded it for them that dwell in the wilderness: they set up the towers thereof, they raised up the palaces thereof; and he brought it to ruin.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "Isa. 13:19."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 59
          },
          {
            "start": 191,
            "end": 194
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Isa. 13:19.",
            "prettyString": "Isaiah 13:19",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "isaiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 13,
                    "end": 13,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 19,
                        "end": 19
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 23:13",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Howl, ye ships of Tarshish: for your strength is laid waste.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 23:14",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And it shall come to pass in that day, that Tyre shall be forgotten seventy years, according to the days of one king: after the end of seventy years shall Tyre sing as an harlot.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 23:15",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Take an harp, go about the city, thou harlot that hast been forgotten; make sweet melody, sing many songs, that thou mayest be remembered.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 23:16",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And it shall come to pass after the end of seventy years, that the Lord will visit Tyre, and she shall turn to her hire, and shall commit fornication with all the kingdoms of the world upon the face of the earth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 107,
            "text": "OR return."
          },
          {
            "start": 138,
            "end": 149,
            "text": "Rev. 18:3 (3, 9)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 23:17",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "And her merchandise and her hire shall be holiness to the Lord: it shall not be treasured nor laid up; for her merchandise shall be for them that dwell before the Lord, to eat sufficiently, and for durable clothing.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "IE Any success she has will only be as permitted by the Lord."
          },
